    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nForkin Earls Property are delighted to present No. 69 Fernhill to the market. Extending to approximately 109 sq.m. (1173 sq.ft.), This well-presented four-bedroom terraced residence offers spacious and well-proportioned accommodation throughout, providing a comfortable family home in a mature and convenient residential setting.\n\nThe accommodation is well proportioned throughout and comprises a welcoming entrance hall, spacious living room, family room, generous kitchen/dining room, utility and shower room on the ground floor. Upstairs, there are three bedrooms, a family bathroom and landing with hot press, providing comfortable and practical accommodation ideally suited to modern family living.\n\nFernhill is a well-established development ideally located within easy reach of Arklow Town Centre. A wide variety of amenities are close at hand, including supermarkets, schools, cafés, restaurants, local shops and an excellent selection of sporting and recreational facilities.\n\nArklow's attractive coastal setting provides plenty of opportunities to enjoy the outdoors, with nearby beaches, riverside walks, golf courses and scenic walking routes. The town is also exceptionally well connected, with regular bus and rail services to Dublin and surrounding areas, while Junction 21 of the M11 motorway is just a short drive away, offering convenient access for those commuting north or south.\n\nCombining generous accommodation within an established residential setting and excellent access to the town's amenities and transport links, No. 69 Fernhill represents an excellent opportunity for those seeking a well-located family home in Arklow.\n\nViewings are highly recommended and by appointment only!"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - - 3.64m x 1.95m\nA bright and welcoming entrance hall with tiled flooring, natural timber finishes and carpeted staircase leading to the first floor. The hallway provides access to the principal ground-floor accommodation.\n\nLiving Room - - 3.64m x 4.48m\nA bright and spacious living room featuring laminate wooden flooring, a large front-facing window providing plenty of natural light, and an attractive feature fireplace with tiled hearth.\n\nKitchen/Dining - - 3.55m x 6.53m\nA spacious kitchen/dining room featuring tiled flooring, a range of fitted timber wall and floor units with ample worktop space, tiled splashback and integrated oven and hob. A large window provides excellent natural light, while the adjoining dining area offers generous space for family dining and entertaining.\n\nFamily Room - - 5.00m x 2.58m\nA bright and versatile family room featuring laminate wooden flooring, timber skirting and a large front-facing window allowing for an abundance of natural light. An ideal additional living space suitable for a variety of uses.\n\nUtility Room - - 3.47m x 2.42m\nA generous utility room with tiled flooring, fitted worktop, plumbing for a washing machine and a window providing natural light. The room also benefits from direct access to the rear garden.\n\nShower Room - - \nA practical ground-floor shower room, fully tiled and comprising a corner shower enclosure, pedestal wash hand basin and WC.\n\nLanding - - 2.81m x 2.51m\nA bright first-floor landing with carpeted flooring, providing access to all three bedrooms and the family bathroom. The landing also benefits from a hot press offering additional storage.\n\nBedroom 1 - - 3.54m x 3.64m\nA spacious double bedroom featuring laminate wooden flooring, timber skirting and alarge window providing plenty of natural light.\n\nBedroom 2 - - 3.01m x 3.08m\nA well-proportioned double bedroom featuring laminate wooden flooring, timber skirting and a large window overlooking the rear garden, allowing for plenty of natural light.\n\nBedroom 3 - - 2.62m x 2.82m\nA bright single bedroom featuring laminate wooden flooring, timber skirting and a large window providing plenty of natural light. Ideal for use as a child's bedroom, guest room or home office.\n\nFamily Bathroom - - 1.67m x 2.49m\nA well-appointed family bathroom with tiled flooring and walls, comprising a bath with overhead shower and screen, pedestal wash hand basin and WC. Two windows provide plenty of natural light.\n\nGarden - \nA generous and private rear garden, predominantly laid to lawn and bordered by mature trees and established planting. The garden also benefits from a gravelled area and useful outdoor storage, offering excellent potential to create an attractive outdoor space.\n\nServices - \nOil fired central heating.Mains Water, Sewage and Electricity.Fibre Internet, Telephone and Satellite in the area.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Spacious four-bed family home, extending to c. 109 sq.m. (1173 sq.ft.).</li><li> Presented in excellent condition throughout.</li><li> Generous rear garden with ample outdoor space.</li><li> Within walking distance to Arklow Town Centre and all its local amenities.</li><li> Excellent transport links with easy access to the M11 motorway, bus and rail services.</ul>"
      },
